@startuml 5a-state-assignment
!include _style.iuml
title EduFlow — State Machine: Assignment (publication state)

[*] --> Draft : teacher saves\n/ create()

state Draft : invisible to students\nall fields editable
state Published : visible to recipients\naccepts submissions
state Closed : visible, read-only\nno new submissions
state Cancelled : hidden from students\nfinal

Draft --> Draft : edit
Draft --> Published : publish\n[due date set if submission required]\n/ published_at = now,\nnotify recipients
Draft --> Cancelled : cancel

Published --> Published : edit\n/ new recipients notified;\ndeadline change notified
Published --> Closed : close\n/ closed_at = now
Published --> Cancelled : cancel\n/ notify recipients

Closed --> Published : reopen

Cancelled --> [*]

note bottom of Published
  Each student's submission has its own
  state machine (see 5b). Publication
  state and submission state are separate.
end note
@enduml
